 # 37\. The Importance of Anti-Sycophancy Design

 Because sycophancy can produce alignment with the user's stated position rather than with the available evidence, systems intended for consequential planning should avoid rewarding agreement merely because agreement is conversationally satisfying.

 Research has found sycophancy across advanced LLMs and has associated it with shifts in user judgment and dependence.  Microsoft+1

 An effective planning assistant should therefore be capable of saying, in substance:

 > “Your proposed premise may be incorrect.”

 and:

 > “The available evidence does not establish that conclusion.”

 and:

 > “There are alternative explanations that should be considered.”

 This is not hostility toward the user.

 It is epistemic independence.

