 # 40\. Security Through Epistemic Diversity

 A broader principle follows from the analysis.

 Security systems often emphasize technical redundancy.

 AI-assisted decision systems also require **epistemic redundancy**.

 Technical redundancy asks:

 > “What happens if this component fails?”

 Epistemic redundancy asks:

 > “What happens if our interpretation of the situation is wrong?”

 The latter requires multiple ways of representing the problem.

 That may include:

 - independent analysts;
- separate data sources;
- alternative models;
- adversarial review;
- domain experts;
- historical comparison;
- scenario analysis.

 The goal is not to guarantee agreement.

 It is to prevent one mistaken representation from becoming universally authoritative.

