 # 42\. A Proposed Taxonomy of Failure

 AI-assisted planning failures can be classified as follows.

 | Failure type | Description |
| --- | --- |
| **Factual failure** | Incorrect underlying information |
| **Representational failure** | Incorrect characterization of the situation |
| **Inferential failure** | Incorrect conclusion from otherwise accurate information |
| **Planning failure** | Plan does not satisfy actual requirements or constraints |
| **Reliance failure** | User accepts an inappropriate model output |
| **Execution failure** | Correct plan is incorrectly implemented |
| **Feedback failure** | New evidence is misinterpreted because of the original skew |
| **Governance failure** | System lacks appropriate oversight or accountability |

These failures can occur independently or in combination.

 The particularly dangerous case is:

 $$
\text{factual}
\rightarrow
\text{representational}
\rightarrow
\text{planning}
\rightarrow
\text{reliance}
\rightarrow
\text{execution}
\rightarrow
\text{feedback}.
$$

